@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
' '   description:  10+ object distributed-system collaboration with multiple link types, branching numbering, and iterators.
'   usecase:      Teach multiple link types, branching message numbering, and iterator markers.
'   complexity:   complex
'   domain:       distributed-systems
' ============================================================================
title Example Communication - Complex Distributed Collaboration

actor "Client" as Client
participant "Gateway" as Gateway
participant "AuthSvc" as AuthSvc
participant "OrderSvc" as OrderSvc
participant "InventorySvc" as InventorySvc
participant "PricingSvc" as PricingSvc
participant "PaymentSvc" as PaymentSvc
participant "ShippingSvc" as ShippingSvc
participant "AuditSvc" as AuditSvc
participant "Cache" as Cache
database "DB" as DB

' LINK TYPES:
'   "--" solid association (persistent structural link)
'   ".." dashed dependency / temporary link
' Different visual styles distinguish durable from transient relationships.

Client -- Gateway
Gateway -- AuthSvc
Gateway -- OrderSvc
OrderSvc -- InventorySvc
OrderSvc -- PricingSvc
OrderSvc -- PaymentSvc
OrderSvc .. ShippingSvc
OrderSvc .. AuditSvc
OrderSvc -- Cache
OrderSvc -- DB

' MESSAGE FLOW with deep nesting and BRANCHING numbering.
' Branching: 2.1a and 2.1b are CONCURRENT sub-calls under message 2.

Client --> Gateway : 1: submitOrder(payload)
Gateway --> AuthSvc : 1.1: verifyToken()
Gateway --> OrderSvc : 2: placeOrder()

' ITERATOR MARKER: "*" prefix means "for each item in a collection".
' The message fires once PER element of the iterated set.
OrderSvc --> InventorySvc : 2.1a: reserveItem()*[for each line item]
OrderSvc --> PricingSvc : 2.1b: calculateTotals()

OrderSvc --> DB : 2.2: persistOrder()
OrderSvc --> Cache : 2.3: warmCache(orderId)

OrderSvc --> PaymentSvc : 3: chargeCard()

' BRANCH on a guard — only one of 3.1a / 3.1b fires depending on the result.
PaymentSvc --> OrderSvc : 3.1a: paymentApproved()
PaymentSvc --> OrderSvc : 3.1b: paymentDeclined()[auth_failed]

' Downstream fan-out on the success branch.
OrderSvc --> ShippingSvc : 4: scheduleShipment()
OrderSvc --> AuditSvc : 5: logTransaction()
Gateway --> Client : 6: returnConfirmation()

' TEACHING NOTES:
'   - "*" iterator marker = the message is sent once per element of a set.
'   - "a"/"b" suffixes (2.1a, 2.1b) denote CONCURRENT sibling calls.
'   - Guards ([auth_failed]) make a message conditional.
'   - Solid vs dashed links distinguish durable associations from transient
'     dependencies — a key structural insight that sequence diagrams hide.
@enduml
